window.docContents[229].resolve({"/Abstraction/Properties/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Properties":{"contents":"A well typed program has a derivation, does not terminate, or is stuck. It is stuck at a case C++17 leaves undefined, or at the end of a main without return, and the evaluator reports it as error. Every well typed constructor has an evaluation rule, checked by inspection of the rule set. There is no Lean proof yet.\n\nEvery construct has rules with mutually exclusive premises, and a Core C++ program has at most one result. The evaluation order fixed left to right removes the choice C++17 leaves to the compiler. The relations of  make the statement precise. Two derivations of  for the same  give the same  and . There is no Lean proof yet.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Abstraction","header":"5.6. Properties","id":"/Abstraction/Properties/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Properties"}});